{
  "case_id": "2022-21-707",
  "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Students for Fair Admissions, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRAWBRIDGE: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: Racial classifications are wrong. That principle was enshrined in our law at great cost following the Civil War. A century of resistance to race neutrality followed, but this Court's landmark decision in Brown finally and firmly rejected the view that racial classifications have any role to play in providing educational opportunities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We will hear argument first this morning in Case 21-707, Students for Fair Admissions versus the University of North Carolina."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Strawbridge, can I take you back to Justice Sotomayor's question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Where?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRAWBRIDGE: We do not think that the university has made a commitment to race-neutral alternatives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Your position will put a lot of pressure going forward, if it's accepted, on what qualifies as race-neutral in the first place. You said socioeconomic is race-neutral. Top 10 percent plan, race-neutral. Is -- you want to respond to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRAWBRIDGE: I think descendants of slaves is a very difficult question because it's so -- it's so highly correlated with race in the history of our country. I'm not sure that any college has proposed that kind of a preference. It would have to --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court basically conflated the educational benefits of diversity, which is actually the interest that -- that Grutter recognizes, with raw representation on campus."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: You're asking us to overrule Grutter, but first want to understand what you think Grutter itself means. It -- it had language in there about a 25-year limit. The decision was in 2003. The current admissions cycle is for the class of '27. It's going to be too late to do anything about that cycle. The next is the class of '28."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "measure their standard as to what they could achieve by race-neutral alternatives by whether they can replicate the precise level of diversity today. So I think that is a form of"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: And -- and --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- the difficulty you're having answering some of these questions about end point were probably in the mind of Justice O'Connor when she wrote the opinion in Grutter for the majority and, as Justice Barrett said, indicated that these racial classifications are potentially dangerous and -- and must have a logical end point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Could you explain how that works?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "University of North Carolina",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PARK: So the expert evidence in our case suggests that around 1.2 percent of the applicant pool as -- as a whole is affected by our race-conscious admissions program."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 104,
        "start": 104
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I'd like to ask you just a hypothetical about narrow tailoring because we're in strict scrutiny land here, and the university has to demonstrate it's narrowly tailored, race is narrowly tailored."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0005-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 107,
        "start": 107
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Is there compelling interest in a squash team composed of really good players or a new art museum? Is that what you're suggesting?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PARK",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0005-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PARK: Right. Right. And I think the other condition I would try to sneak in is that there wouldn't be a --a material negative impact on the academic environment. And -- and -- and third is that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. PARK",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0005-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PARK: My understanding is that just like other situations where they might not fit within the particular boxes on the Common Application, that we rely on self-reporting and we would ask -- you know, they can volunteer their particular country of origin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0005-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 119,
        "start": 119
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Hinojosa, if this were a Title VI case and there was an allegation of discrimination against the University of North Carolina, who would bear the burden of coming forward?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0005-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 123,
        "start": 123
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Their own expert said that racial diversity was an important compelling interest, didn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hinojosa",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0006-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 131,
        "start": 131
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "race-conscious admissions programs at -- well, universities that have race-conscious admissions programs actually have lesser degree of stigma attached, you know, both internal for the student and external, what they're hearing from other students --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0006-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 132,
        "start": 132
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How -- what benefits academically are there to your definition or your -- the -- the diversity that you're asserting specifically?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Elizabeth B. Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0006-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 145,
        "start": 145
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For decades, this Court has rightly recognized that student body diversity is a compelling interest that can justify limited consideration of race in university admissions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Elizabeth B. Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0006-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 147,
        "start": 147
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is the suite of benefits that the Court's precedents have already recognized, things like increasing cross-racial understanding, which can have direct impacts on challenging stereotypes and assumptions and leading to positive developments with cognitive development that can be perceived as early as a student's second year in college."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, it is critically important to the military to be able to achieve diverse student bodies in the service academies, but it's also critically important, because, actually, more officers come from ROTC programs, to try to protect and preserve space for universities to also achieve the educational benefits of diversity and provide the paths to leadership that inhere in those programs as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 156,
        "start": 156
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now virtually all of the states that have banned consideration of race in any respect experienced a dramatic drop in enrollment of unrepresented minority students, particularly Black students and Native American students, but particularly Black students."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 162,
        "start": 162
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what would a committed originalist think about the kind of race-consciousness that's at issue here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 164,
        "start": 164
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Where --where did Justice Stevens err?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 164,
        "start": 164
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In not recognizing that the term \"discrimination\" in this context is ambiguous."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0007-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 169,
        "start": 169
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, when it allows for meaningful representation and meaningful diversity on those campuses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0008-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 170,
        "start": 170
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But, if you don't have a number, and I understand why it's difficult, and I understand the problems with that, I get all that, but if you don't have something measurable, it's going to be very hard for this Court, if we're called upon 10 years from now or 20 years from now, it's going to be -- you know, this is a bit of a replay of the Grutter argument, but if we come back to it, okay, are we there yet? What do we look at? You're saying meaningful opportunity. I don't know exactly what that means. I don't know how the schools will know when they have to -- when they've -- you know -- the -- the -- when the race-neutral alternative could get them close enough or -- it has to meet some threshold. I don't know what \"meaningful\" means."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0008-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 175,
        "start": 175
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL PRELOGAR: I think that because they involve racial classifications, it is necessary to test them under strict scrutiny. And so we're not suggesting that under an originalist case, they would just be automatically exempt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Strawbridge",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0008-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 179,
        "start": 179
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STRAWBRIDGE: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. I'm going to try to make four points here. First, with respect to the military, the -- the United States brief on that is long on assertions that race-neutral alternatives are not available to it and would not work but not actually long on any evidence of that fact. We don't know precisely what race-neutral alternatives they have looked at. We don't know what has been tried. We don't know what else could be available to them, especially with the fact that they can draw on appointed -- appointments from the enlisted ranks, as well as from prep schools."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-707",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b15032ff7827658d503ef1087aa78dc56f35de3a163b964b11132e73ef0c82c0",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b15032ff7827-0008-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 183,
        "start": 183
      },
